SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:storytime,library,baby,toddler,family,Arts & Culture,Music
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: OCPL - Aliso Viejo Branch\\nCost: free\\nAges: 0-60
  months\\nCategory: Music & Dance\\n\\nJoin us for a cultural presentation
  of Pre-Civil War-era music by the Rigo Moreno Quintet. Complementing the 
 library's reading of James by Percival Everett\, the performance will focu
 s on the musical culture and experience of Black Americans during that tim
 e period. The performance will feature a variety of spirituals\, slave son
 gs\, work songs\, and blues. The presentation will also include several sh
 ort excerpts explaining the historical relevance and importance of each mu
 sical piece.\n\nThis project is funded in part through a grant from the Ca
 lifornia Department of Aging and administered locally by the Orange County
  Office on Aging.\\n\\nMore info: https://ocpl.libcal.com/event/16746984
LOCATION:Aliso Viejo\, Aliso Viejo
URL:https://ocpl.libcal.com/event/16746984
