BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[FREE] Regulation Station Workshop: Beneath the Behavior
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260615T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260615T183000
DTSTAMP:20260603T124514Z
UID:df162a5f11bbc554007a99fa8a775a0b@family-events-agent
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:storytime,library,baby,toddler,family,Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: OCPL - Tustin Branch\\nCost: free\\nAges: 0-60 mont
 hs\\nCategory: Storytime\\n\\nWhat if challenging behaviors are actually c
 lues? In this interactive workshop\, pediatric occupational and speech the
 rapists from Irvine Therapy Services will help parents look beyond meltdow
 ns\, big emotions\, and shutdowns to better understand what may be happeni
 ng beneath the surface. Learn how sensory processing\, communication diffe
 rences\, and nervous system regulation shape behavior\, and leave with pra
 ctical strategies to support your child through connection\, understanding
 \, and co-regulation.\n\nJennie Ni\, MS\, OTR/L: Jennie brings 25 years of
  experience and a relationship-based\, play-driven approach to occupationa
 l therapy\, grounded in deep respect for each child’s unique nervous sys
 tem. She focuses on creating safe\, supportive\, and co-regulated interact
 ions where children feel free to explore\, take risks\, and discover new w
 ays of engaging with their world.\n\nAmanda Harpst\, MS\, CCC-SLP: Amanda 
 brings 22 years of experience and a developmental\, relationship-based app
 roach to speech therapy that is neurodiversity-affirming\, strengths-based
 \, child-directed\, and deeply family-centered. She believes meaningful co
 mmunication grows through connection\, play\, and trust—and works intent
 ionally to support each child’s unique communication profile in ways tha
 t feel safe\, joyful\, and motivating.\n\nNo registration required. For mo
 re information\, email ocpl.programs@occr.ocgov.com.\\n\\nMore info: https
 ://ocpl.libcal.com/event/16963573
LOCATION:Tustin\, Tustin
URL:https://ocpl.libcal.com/event/16963573
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Tomorrow: Regulation Station Workshop: Beneath the Behavior
TRIGGER:-P1D
END:VALARM
