SUMMARY:[FREE] Regulation Station Workshop: Understanding Your Sensory Pre
 ferences
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260624T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260624T183000
DTSTAMP:20260603T124514Z
UID:398d6be3a37589cd86a93f5ee2bb3387@family-events-agent
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:storytime,library,baby,toddler,family,Diversity,Equity & Inclus
 ion,Guest Speaker,Health & Wellness,Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: OCPL - El Toro Branch\\nCost: free\\nAges: 0-60 mon
 ths\\nCategory: Music & Dance\\n\\nEver wonder why certain sounds\, textur
 es\, or environments feel instantly calming or completely overwhelming? Th
 is interactive workshop explores how sensory processing shapes your daily 
 experiences\, energy\, and regulation. You’ll learn about the different 
 sensory systems\, who they impact (hint: everyone)\, and take part in play
 ful\, hands-on experiments to better understand your own sensory preferenc
 es. You’ll also leave with a practical handout to help you make sense of
  your unique sensory preferences and use them to support your well-being.\
 \n\\nMore info: https://ocpl.libcal.com/event/16935654
LOCATION:El Toro\, El Toro
URL:https://ocpl.libcal.com/event/16935654
